s","api_error_status":null,"result":"I added the Panel Grid component in `PanelGridComponent.cs` and `dotnet build` succeeds with 0 errors. The only warnings are about which Grasshopper package version got picked, and they were there before my change. I haven't run it inside Grasshopper, so nothing beyond the build has been tested.\n\nIt follows the same layout as `AddComponent.cs`, under Bench → Panels, with the five inputs, four outputs and defaults you listed.\n\nChoices I made where the spec left room:\n- **Order:** \"U first then V\" is the outer loop, so panel number = U cell × V Count + V cell. If you meant V to step fastest, it's a one-line swap of the two loops.\n- **Corner order:** each panel runs (u0,v0) → (u1,v0) → (u1,v1) → (u0,v1) and back to the start.\n- **Inset:** each corner moves toward the average of the four corners by Inset. If a corner is already closer than that, it lands on the average instead of passing it. Area and Deviation are worked out from the inset corners, not the original ones.\n- **Area:** the triangles are (corner 0, 1, 2) and (corner 0, 2, 3).\n- **Flat-panel edge case:** if the first three corners lie on a straight line there's no single plane through them, so Deviation is set to 0.\n- **Strictness:** a panel only counts as Non Planar when its Deviation is strictly greater than Tolerance.\n- **Trimmed surfaces:** if you plug in a trimmed surface, the grid covers the whole untrimmed surface and ignores the trim.\n- **Messages:** each invalid input gets its own error. The warning reads, for example, \"3 panels are not planar within tolerance 0.01.\"","ttft_ms":3131,"type":"result","duration_ms":42879,"uuid":"63de5524-d79b-46bd-b747-ae943467f0ef","ttft_stream_ms":2142,"time_to_request_ms":242,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":4,"system_prompt":134,"resume_other":1,"process_user_input":2,"input_attachments":14,"input_hooks":1,"conversation_append":1,"tool_pool_refresh":2,"init_message":40,"init_frame_send":3,"engine_pickup":1,"l